 1. Disclamer

 This program is Freeware, but it may only be spread in it's original archive.
 The author takes no blaim, if there is any harm to your computer, HD, Tron BBS
 or other things that may occour whem using this program.




 2. What is it?

 This program generates New files from you Filecatalog and put them in an ascii
 file....



 3. How to install it

 Well the install part is very simple, just copy the directorys from this 
 archive to the right dirs in your Tron BBS directory...

 

 4. The Config file

 The config file: NewFiles.cfg in the Tron:cfg/ directory, is build with three
 lines.
 
 The First line is the day count... This is the number the program uses to
 calculate the count back for the newfiles. 

 The daycount in the original archive is 7, wich means that TNF creates a ascii
 file with all the new files since the last 7 days.

 The second line is a path+filename for the bbs add. This file will be on top
 of your New Files list. 

 The path in the orginal archive is Tron:Text/BBSadd.asc

 The third line is for the logfile... If you put 'on' on this line, TNF will
 create a logfile in the Tron:log directory.. 

 If you put 'off' on this line, TNF won't create a logfile and the program will
 be a little faster




 5. How to start it

 Well you can run it from Cli or from a Cron utility like Cybercron..

 

 6. What the program does

 The program reads the Tron:cfg/Allfiles.cfg and uses this to make the Newfiles
 ascii file. The program uses the file areas you've put in this config.

 example: SECTIONS  1-100 , 30
          SECTIONS  40-50

 if you made a config to make more than 1 allfiles list, the program will use
 that too.

 The program will make the files in the temp directory you have in your 
 Tron:cfg/Allfiles.cfg. The files wich are created will not move from that
 directory, so if your temp dir is RAM:, you can copy them to HD later.

 The filename the program uses is NewFiles.txtX, where X is the number of
 the Newfiles list.



 7. Future of this program

 Well i have some ideas:

 - Automatic mail config, so the Newfiles.txt will be put in a mail area
 - Archive it and put in on the BBS, like TAF does.



